It _can_, yeah, but that's pretty darned ugly.  And it doesn't handle
auto-hyphenation for justified text, or gracefully handle varying
column-width terminals, or a lot of the other stuff that *roff will do
for you.

*roff was really designed for flexible text file generation (as well
as printable output).  Things like DocBook can do it well in a modern
SGML/XML manner, and many of them (or *roff) will do nice HTML output
as well.  Using HTML just seems like the wrong tool for the job, to me.


